A proper coloring assigns labels to vertices while separating every adjacent pair. This interactive path begins with easy boundary cases, reveals the local partition behind deletion–contraction, and finishes with independent components. For background, see the [chromatic polynomial](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromatic_polynomial) and [graph coloring](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_coloring).

## 1. Calibrate the count

The empty graph permits every assignment, while the complete graph permits only injections. Adjust both parameters and compare $q^n$ with $q^{\underline n}$.

